/// A module that declares a member named like a predefined class reaches its
/// own member. newspeak-spec.pdf 3.2 has `Object` provide "accessors for
/// predefined classes", so a bare `String` is at most `self String`; but
/// 5.7 first searches the lexically enclosing constructs, and the module
/// declares a method `String`, so the implicit send is `outer
/// ModuleDeclaresString String` and never reaches `Object`'s accessor --
/// 2.3.1: "only if no lexically visible matching method is found, do we
/// proceed up the inheritance chain of self". A regression guard: the
/// lexical member won before `String` became a send, and must still.
class ModuleDeclaresString = Object new () (
  String = (
    ^'mine'.
  )

  public main: platform args: arguments = (
    platform transcript
        show: String;
        newLine.
  )
)
